WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.860
This video was sponsored by The Purge on USA
Network.

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:06.100
A 10 episode television event.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.809
Watch The Purge Tuesdays on USA Network and
stick around to the end of this video if you

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:14.450
want to hear about how this episode sets up
for the events of The Purge: Election Year.

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:21.369
Let’s roll that intro.

00:00:21.369 --> 00:00:23.390
Welcome back to Things You Missed.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:27.810
If it feels like we just Purged a few episodes
ago, it’s because we’re getting over FIVE

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.070
TIMES the Purge coverage this year.

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:33.650
In today’s video, I’ll be breaking down
everything you might have missed in ‘What

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:37.070
Is America?’, the first episode of this
new series.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.960
The first thing we see is a shower head beginning
to dispense water.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.680
This is a significant shot to open on because
one of the ideologies of The Purge, is that

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:47.640
it’s a way for the rich upper-class to cleanse
society of the poor, the homeless and the

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:48.640
mentally ill.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.720
I’ve talked about the reasoning for this
before, but to quickly sum it up, these are

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:55.950
all groups that rely on government money to
fund food-stamps, shelters, etcetera.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:59.519
So The Purge is more of an excuse to remove
these groups; and there are actually many

00:00:59.519 --> 00:01:03.410
instances where these corrupt politicians
actually use the word “cleanse” to describe

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:04.410
The Purge.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.890
So who is this group that’s being cleansed
in the showers?

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:11.630
It’s robed Purge cult , possibly called
The OMF, that we see giving themselves up

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:13.190
Purgers as part of a ritual.

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:15.230
So they are cleansing themselves for this
ritual.

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:18.760
They also show great support for the idea
of The Purge since they have been brainwashed

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:23.320
into believing they are not dying but going
to this place called The Invisible.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:26.610
Ever since The First Purge -- and this takes
place about 10 years after -- blue flowers

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:28.830
have been a symbol of support for The Purge.

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:32.490
The cult displays these flowers outside of
their school, the ones who are being Purged

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:38.060
have blue robes, blue towels, they ride in
a blue school bus and even blue shower scrub

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.060
things.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:40.060
I don’t know what they’re called.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:43.530
It seems that they are allowed to switch from
yellow robes to blue when they are old enough,

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:47.700
as mentioned by the kids Miguel encounters
when looking for his sister, and only after

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:51.580
they’ve taken this ritualistic shower to
cleanse themselves for the Purgers, because

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:55.090
after the shower, they change into the blue
robes, and the yellow robes can be seen hanging

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:56.710
on the hook in the background.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:59.960
In her letter to Miguel, Penelope mentions
that she’ll be joining their parents on

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:01.770
the anniversary of their giving.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:05.250
And then later at the cult training school,
it's revealed that their parents’ lives

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.360
were taken on the night of the very first
Purge.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:11.030
I’m not sure if that’s a reference to
the test Purge that took place on Staten Island

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:14.570
in the movie entitled, The First Purge, or
if they are referring to the first nation-wide

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:16.950
Purge, that would have taken place the year
after that.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:20.310
I’d like to go back and rewatch The First
Purge, and see if there are any references

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:24.480
to the parents or anything, but at the time
of making this video, it’s not out on Blu-Ray

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:28.950
yet, but if you remember anything, or watch
this video later on, please do leave your

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:30.110
findings in the comments.

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:33.970
I also have a theory about why these kids
are willing to sacrifice their lives.

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:38.030
The first place that Miguel goes to try to
find his sister is a rehabilitation center.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:41.500
We don’t know whether she’s a drug addict
or an alcoholic, but either one of these would

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:45.340
put her into the group of people that the
NFFA political party is trying to eliminate.

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:49.650
I think this freaky lady who is the leader
of the cult is an NFFA member who has rounded

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:52.900
up these kids or young adults who are recovering
because they’re in a state where they can

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.350
be easily manipulated.

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:58.180
She then tricks them into believing they are
doing something good by sacrificing themselves

00:02:58.180 --> 00:02:59.240
to the Purge.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:02.730
Another piece of evidence to support that
theory is that in this iteration of The Purge,

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:07.370
we learn the answer to a long-pondered fan
question: what happens to hospitals during

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:08.370
The Purge?

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:11.770
There are always patients who need to be treated,
so you can’t just shut down hospitals for

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:14.220
12 hours the same as you do with emergency
services.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:18.190
It’s been stated in the movies that certain
locations and people are protected, and in

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:21.440
this episode, the protection of hospitals
in confirmed.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:25.680
However, Miguel finds out that the rehabilitation
center his sister had been staying in does

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.140
not have this same protection.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:32.150
This doesn’t make a whole lot of sense from
an operational standpoint, because these patients

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:34.970
could need the same constant care that a hospital
patient would need.

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:37.900
But try looking at it from the NFFA standpoint.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:42.310
Rehab centers are filled with those they don’t
deem fit for society, whereas hospitals will

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:46.290
house some of their own, in fact, only the
rich will be able to afford long hospital

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:49.150
stays, so it makes sense to have them be a
safe haven.

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:53.430
Miguel’s search for his sister eventually
leads him to a set of abandoned buildings.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:57.020
From the outside it would appear they are
still in support of The Purge as you can see

00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:01.550
from the blue flower mural on the wall, skeleton
figures as a sign of death and what appears

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:04.040
to be a caricature of a New Founding Father.

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:07.850
However, the inside looks like it was once
the center of a civil rights movement.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:11.240
There are paintings of civil rights figures
like Martin Luther King Jr.

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:14.740
There are also quotes graffitied on the wall,
such as “I freed a thousand slaves.

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:17.620
I could have freed more if only they knew
they were slaves.”

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:21.709
I looked it up, apparently this is widely
known as a quote by Harriet Tubman, although

00:04:21.709 --> 00:04:24.060
there’s no proof she ever actually said
it.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:25.400
But the meaning still stands.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:30.000
There’s also an MLK quote: “Almost always,
the creative dedicated minority has made the

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.000
world better.”

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:35.620
The name Assata Shakur, who is known for murdering
a state trooper and using violence to further

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:37.939
her agenda, also appears on the wall.

00:04:37.939 --> 00:04:41.960
The second of the three main storylines follows
a woman named Jane who works for an equity

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.250
firm, and is forced to work on Purge night.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:47.720
A private equity firm usually manages investments
funds.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:50.570
Investment funds are similar to The Purge
itself in that they in they involve a pool

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:53.320
of investors taking advantage of the size
of their group.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:57.320
It’s very similar to how the NFFA bands
together to take advantage of the lower class.

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:00.590
Jane is trying to work herself up to a position
of power within the company.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:03.780
When visiting her Mom in the hospital, her
Mom mentions something about Jane needing

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:08.050
to get a promotion, telling her she would
have it if she had just “played the game”.

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:11.570
Jane doesn’t want to talk about it, it seems
like a sore subject, but I’m guessing Jane’s

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:15.430
bosses are corrupt and asked her to take part
in some shady business tactics or possibly

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:16.800
tried to take advantage of her.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:20.220
There is some evidence of her employers’
inappropriate behaviour when one of her bosses

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:24.150
joins the rest of the workers via video call
and Jane calls him out for being the type

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:25.370
of person to eavesdrop.

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:29.370
Then, in the most creepy way possible, he
tells her that he’s always watching and

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:30.370
listening.

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:33.400
Outside of the building she works in, you
can see a sign that reads: “The price of

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:36.270
freedom can be seen fro within these walls.”

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.949
If that’s not a red flag, I don’t know
what is.

00:05:38.949 --> 00:05:41.260
But on Purge night, she’s got some tricks
of her own.

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:45.260
She goes down and makes some kind of transaction
-- it looks like she’s ordering a hit.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:48.590
Judging from the tension between her and her
boss, I’ve gotta guess that she’s ordering

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:49.730
the hit on him.

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:53.400
But my guess is that her boss has cameras
and microphones hidden all over the building,

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.320
and finds out about her hitman.

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:58.680
She thinks she’s safe at work, but if her
boss comes after her, she could actually be

00:05:58.680 --> 00:05:59.680
in great danger.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:04.740
The last storyline follows Jenna and Rick,
a married couple who attend an NFFA party

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:07.480
in order to try to close a deal to get funding
for their business.

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:12.970
As they leave the house, you may notice a
sign in the front yard reading “Sandin Security”.

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:16.640
If you remember back to the original Purge
film, James Sandin, the father of the family

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:20.880
in that movie sold security systems for the
Purge, but his cheap systems came back to

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:24.449
bite him when his neighbors turned against
him for overcharging them on their security

00:06:24.449 --> 00:06:25.449
systems.

00:06:25.449 --> 00:06:29.110
In the end, James was killed, but according
to this sign, his company lived on without

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:30.110
him.

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:33.050
When they arrive at the house, in addition
to the blue flowers, there are eagle statues

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:35.780
that represent the eagle in the NFFA logo.

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:39.930
Once the party begins, the hosts give out
gifts to their guests in the form of Purge

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:40.930
masks.

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:44.690
Each one is a cut-out face of a serial killer,
and when I saw the characters putting these

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:46.930
on I pretty much almost lost it.

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:50.580
They look almost exactly like my FoundFlix
masks that I’ve been wearing during the

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:51.580
Purge.

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:53.970
The cut-out eyes, the expressions, the grayscale.

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:57.389
I mean I wasn’t aware you watched my show,
Mr. Demonaco.

00:06:57.389 --> 00:07:00.290
I’m kidding about that last part of course,
but anyways…

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:04.300
Rick gets David Richard Berkowitz, a serial
killer from the 70s who took out 8 people

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:05.520
in separate attacks.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:10.050
Jenna ends up getting Susan Denise Atkins,
who was a follower of Charles Manson and she

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:12.930
had claimed nine lives back in the summer
of 69.

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:16.889
I’m assuming those were the best days of
her life, because the rest of them were spent

00:07:16.889 --> 00:07:17.889
in jail.

00:07:17.889 --> 00:07:21.380
I’ll be keeping an eye on RIck and Jenna
to see if the masks they recieve end up foreshadowing

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:23.260
anything with their characters.

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:26.800
So that covers all of the Things You Missed
involving the main characters, but before

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:30.690
our Purge time is up, I wanted to point out
some things that could have snuck past you

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:32.790
about the world and the time period.

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:36.970
It’s mentioned on TV that this could the
biggest purge ever, due to the massive amount

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:39.630
of Purge materials sold leading up to it.

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:41.760
Like this guy who buys 12 rolls of toilet
paper.

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:45.880
I mean, I can only imagine he got caught TPing
some house as a kid on Halloween or something,

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:49.470
and so he decided to spend his Purge night
(where he can do literally anything, by the

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:54.169
way) throwing toilet paper on old Ms Jenkins’s
place when there’s nothing she can do about

00:07:54.169 --> 00:07:55.169
it.

00:07:55.169 --> 00:07:58.000
But if the reports are correct and this is
the biggest Purge, it makes sense how this

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:01.990
could lead into The Purge: Election Year,
with people being devastated by the damage

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:05.390
of this year’s Purge and really turning
against the idea, they’d be looking for

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:10.100
a candidate to get behind in the next election,
which would take place in 2032, because Senator

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:14.000
Roan doesn’t win back the White House until
2 elections later in 2040.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:18.789
It’s going to be hard to see from this image,
but if you zoom in on any license plate in

00:08:18.789 --> 00:08:23.250
the show, the state insignia are gone in favor
of a design that says, A Nation Reborn.

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:27.669
I wonder if the 50 State system was somehow
removed by the NFFA in order to keep them

00:08:27.669 --> 00:08:28.669
in power.

00:08:28.669 --> 00:08:32.380
Another note on the current political situation,
America is currently at war.

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:35.689
When Miguel explains that he just got back
from the Marines, one of the guys chimes in

00:08:35.689 --> 00:08:37.729
and asks why he isn’t off fighting still.

00:08:37.729 --> 00:08:41.099
So although we do know that a war is still
going on, we don’t really know any of the

00:08:41.099 --> 00:08:42.099
details.

00:08:42.099 --> 00:08:45.709
The last thing to note, is that something
major happened in last year’s Purge.

00:08:45.709 --> 00:08:49.319
As Jane signs in at her office, the following
can be heard on the radio in the background:

00:08:49.319 --> 00:08:52.399
“We’ll see if any clever Purgers are able
to duplicate last year’s epic Purge night

00:08:52.399 --> 00:08:59.550
heist of Southern Holdisback, where four masked
murderers were able to get away with twelve

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:00.550
counts of…”

00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:04.430
We’ll see if any clever Purgers are able
to duplicate last year’s epic Purge night

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:08.689
heist of Southern Holdisback, where four masked
murderers were able to get away with twelve

00:09:08.689 --> 00:09:10.360
counts of…

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:13.310
And that’s all we can really hear, but it
will be interesting to see if we learn more

00:09:13.310 --> 00:09:14.310
about that.

00:09:14.310 --> 00:09:18.220
If you are interested in learning more, there
are 9 more episodes of The Purge lined up

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:20.449
for you, Tuesdays on USA Network.

00:09:20.449 --> 00:09:22.379
The only question is, will you hide?

00:09:22.379 --> 00:09:23.779
Or will you seek?

00:09:23.779 --> 00:09:28.119
Be sure to tune in next and see if you can
spot the Happy Death Day reference they dropped

00:09:28.119 --> 00:09:29.470
in the second episode.

00:09:29.470 --> 00:09:33.110
If you’re excited to see that, go ahead
and leave a like on this video.

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:36.550
And make sure you’re up to date on all the
Things You might have missed in your favorite

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:38.000
horror franchises.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:42.600
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, ring that deathbell for

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:46.499
notifications and I’ll see you in the next
one.

00:09:46.499 --> 00:09:48.630
Assuming we both survive.

